%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a85fc328da289904f9128118aaa30453, type: 3}
  m_Name: Archive_Topic_Catalog
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::LogicLegends.OpenArchive.Topics.ArchiveTopicCatalog
  propositions:
  - title: Conjunction
    questions:
    - questionText: It is only true when both statements are true.
      options:
      - Exclusive OR
      - Conjunction
      - Biconditional
      - Disjunction
      correctOptionIndex: 1
    - questionText: Both statements must be true for the whole statement to be true.
      options:
      - Conjunction
      - Exclusive OR
      - Biconditional
      - Disjunction
      correctOptionIndex: 0
    - questionText: I combine two statements using the word AND.
      options:
      - Exclusive OR
      - Biconditional
      - Conjunction
      - Disjunction
      correctOptionIndex: 2
    - questionText: If even one of the two statements is false, the entire statement
        becomes false.
      options:
      - Exclusive OR
      - Biconditional
      - Disjunction
      - Conjunction
      correctOptionIndex: 3
    - questionText: Given P and Q, I am true only when P is true and Q is true.
      options:
      - Exclusive OR
      - Conjunction
      - Biconditional
      - Disjunction
      correctOptionIndex: 1
    - questionText: "My symbol is \u2227, and I require both sides to hold true."
      options:
      - Conjunction
      - Exclusive OR
      - Biconditional
      - Disjunction
      correctOptionIndex: 0
    - questionText: P ___ Q is true only for TT. It is false for TF, FT and FF. Which
        connective belongs in the blank?
      options:
      - Exclusive OR
      - Biconditional
      - Conjunction
      - Disjunction
      correctOptionIndex: 2
    - questionText: 'Four possibilities exist: TT, TF, FT, and FF. Only TT gives
        me a true result.'
      options:
      - Exclusive OR
      - Biconditional
      - Disjunction
      - Conjunction
      correctOptionIndex: 3
    - questionText: The gate opens only if you possess the key AND activate the switch.
        Which logical operation does this represent?
      options:
      - Exclusive OR
      - Conjunction
      - Biconditional
      - Disjunction
      correctOptionIndex: 1
    - questionText: "Two conditions guard the path. Satisfying only one is not enough\u2014you
        must satisfy both."
      options:
      - Conjunction
      - Exclusive OR
      - Biconditional
      - Disjunction
      correctOptionIndex: 0
  - title: Disjunction
    questions:
    - questionText: It is true when at least one statement is true.
      options:
      - Conjunction
      - Exclusive OR
      - Disjunction
      - Biconditional
      correctOptionIndex: 2
    - questionText: 'I combine statements using inclusive OR: either may be true,
        and both may be true.'
      options:
      - Conjunction
      - Exclusive OR
      - Biconditional
      - Disjunction
      correctOptionIndex: 3
    - questionText: I am false only when both statements are false.
      options:
      - Disjunction
      - Conjunction
      - Exclusive OR
      - Biconditional
      correctOptionIndex: 0
    - questionText: Given P and Q, I am true if P is true, Q is true, or both are
        true.
      options:
      - Conjunction
      - Disjunction
      - Exclusive OR
      - Biconditional
      correctOptionIndex: 1
    - questionText: "My symbol is \u2228. At least one statement must be true; both
        true is also allowed."
      options:
      - Conjunction
      - Exclusive OR
      - Disjunction
      - Biconditional
      correctOptionIndex: 2
    - questionText: P ___ Q is true for TT, TF and FT, but false for FF. Which connective
        belongs in the blank?
      options:
      - Conjunction
      - Exclusive OR
      - Biconditional
      - Disjunction
      correctOptionIndex: 3
    - questionText: 'Four possibilities exist: TT, TF, FT, and FF. I am true in every
        case except FF.'
      options:
      - Disjunction
      - Conjunction
      - Exclusive OR
      - Biconditional
      correctOptionIndex: 0
    - questionText: The gate opens if you possess the key OR know the secret code.
        Either condition is enough. Which logical operation does this represent?
      options:
      - Conjunction
      - Disjunction
      - Exclusive OR
      - Biconditional
      correctOptionIndex: 1
    - questionText: Two paths can activate the mechanism. Either path may succeed,
        and activating both also works.
      options:
      - Conjunction
      - Exclusive OR
      - Disjunction
      - Biconditional
      correctOptionIndex: 2
    - questionText: You don't need both conditions to succeed. One true condition
        is enough, but two true conditions work as well.
      options:
      - Conjunction
      - Exclusive OR
      - Biconditional
      - Disjunction
      correctOptionIndex: 3
  - title: Exclusive OR
    questions:
    - questionText: It is true only when exactly one statement is true.
      options:
      - Disjunction
      - Biconditional
      - Conjunction
      - Exclusive OR
      correctOptionIndex: 3
    - questionText: I am true exactly when one statement is true and the other is
        false. I am false when their truth values match.
      options:
      - Exclusive OR
      - Disjunction
      - Biconditional
      - Conjunction
      correctOptionIndex: 0
    - questionText: If both statements have the same truth value, I become false.
      options:
      - Disjunction
      - Exclusive OR
      - Biconditional
      - Conjunction
      correctOptionIndex: 1
    - questionText: Given P and Q, I am true when P is true or Q is true, but not
        both.
      options:
      - Disjunction
      - Biconditional
      - Exclusive OR
      - Conjunction
      correctOptionIndex: 2
    - questionText: I require the two statements to have different truth values for
        the result to be true.
      options:
      - Disjunction
      - Biconditional
      - Conjunction
      - Exclusive OR
      correctOptionIndex: 3
    - questionText: P is true and Q is false. The resulting statement is true. But
        if both become true, the result becomes false.
      options:
      - Exclusive OR
      - Disjunction
      - Biconditional
      - Conjunction
      correctOptionIndex: 0
    - questionText: 'Four possibilities exist: TT, TF, FT, and FF. Only TF and FT
        make me true.'
      options:
      - Disjunction
      - Exclusive OR
      - Biconditional
      - Conjunction
      correctOptionIndex: 1
    - questionText: Two switches control the gate. Activate either one to open it,
        but activating both will keep it closed.
      options:
      - Disjunction
      - Biconditional
      - Exclusive OR
      - Conjunction
      correctOptionIndex: 2
    - questionText: You may choose the sword or the shield, but choosing both will
        not satisfy the condition.
      options:
      - Disjunction
      - Biconditional
      - Conjunction
      - Exclusive OR
      correctOptionIndex: 3
    - questionText: 'I resemble OR, but there is one important restriction: both
        statements cannot be true at the same time.'
      options:
      - Exclusive OR
      - Disjunction
      - Biconditional
      - Conjunction
      correctOptionIndex: 0
  - title: Conditional
    questions:
    - questionText: It is false only when the first statement is true and the second
        statement is false
      options:
      - Conditional
      - Conjunction
      - Biconditional
      - Exclusive OR
      correctOptionIndex: 0
    - questionText: 'I connect two statements in the form: If P, then Q.'
      options:
      - Conjunction
      - Conditional
      - Biconditional
      - Exclusive OR
      correctOptionIndex: 1
    - questionText: 'I make a promise: whenever the first statement is true, the
        second statement must also be true.'
      options:
      - Conjunction
      - Biconditional
      - Conditional
      - Exclusive OR
      correctOptionIndex: 2
    - questionText: "Given P and Q, I am written as P \u2192 Q."
      options:
      - Conjunction
      - Biconditional
      - Exclusive OR
      - Conditional
      correctOptionIndex: 3
    - questionText: My only false case is P true and Q false. In all three other
        cases I am true. Which connective am I?
      options:
      - Conditional
      - Conjunction
      - Biconditional
      - Exclusive OR
      correctOptionIndex: 0
    - questionText: 'Four possibilities exist: TT, TF, FT, and FF. Only TF makes
        me false.'
      options:
      - Conjunction
      - Conditional
      - Biconditional
      - Exclusive OR
      correctOptionIndex: 1
    - questionText: P is true and Q is true, so 'If P, then Q' is satisfied. Which
        logical operation does this represent?
      options:
      - Conjunction
      - Biconditional
      - Conditional
      - Exclusive OR
      correctOptionIndex: 2
    - questionText: If you defeat the guardian, then the gate will open. Which logical
        operation describes this condition?
      options:
      - Conjunction
      - Biconditional
      - Exclusive OR
      - Conditional
      correctOptionIndex: 3
    - questionText: 'The rule says: If the torch is lit, then the hidden passage
        will appear.'
      options:
      - Conditional
      - Conjunction
      - Biconditional
      - Exclusive OR
      correctOptionIndex: 0
    - questionText: "My symbol is \u2192. The statement before me is the condition,
        while the statement after me is the consequence."
      options:
      - Conjunction
      - Conditional
      - Biconditional
      - Exclusive OR
      correctOptionIndex: 1
  - title: Biconditional
    questions:
    - questionText: It is true when both statements have the same truth value.
      options:
      - Biconditional
      - Conjunction
      - Conditional
      - Exclusive OR
      correctOptionIndex: 0
    - questionText: I am true when both statements are true or when both statements
        are false.
      options:
      - Conjunction
      - Biconditional
      - Conditional
      - Exclusive OR
      correctOptionIndex: 1
    - questionText: I become false whenever the two statements have different truth
        values.
      options:
      - Conjunction
      - Conditional
      - Biconditional
      - Exclusive OR
      correctOptionIndex: 2
    - questionText: "Given P and Q, I am written as P \u2194 Q."
      options:
      - Conjunction
      - Conditional
      - Exclusive OR
      - Biconditional
      correctOptionIndex: 3
    - questionText: I connect two statements where each one implies the other.
      options:
      - Biconditional
      - Conjunction
      - Conditional
      - Exclusive OR
      correctOptionIndex: 0
    - questionText: 'Four possibilities exist: TT, TF, FT, and FF. Only TT and FF
        make me true.'
      options:
      - Conjunction
      - Biconditional
      - Conditional
      - Exclusive OR
      correctOptionIndex: 1
    - questionText: P is true and Q is true, so the statement is true. If both become
        false, the statement remains true.
      options:
      - Conjunction
      - Conditional
      - Biconditional
      - Exclusive OR
      correctOptionIndex: 2
    - questionText: The gate opens if the two magical switches are either both activated
        or both deactivated.
      options:
      - Conjunction
      - Conditional
      - Exclusive OR
      - Biconditional
      correctOptionIndex: 3
    - questionText: The two conditions must agree. If one is true while the other
        is false, the condition fails.
      options:
      - Biconditional
      - Conjunction
      - Conditional
      - Exclusive OR
      correctOptionIndex: 0
    - questionText: "My symbol is \u2194, and I express that one statement is true
        exactly when the other statement is true."
      options:
      - Conjunction
      - Biconditional
      - Conditional
      - Exclusive OR
      correctOptionIndex: 1
